        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### What the slider published\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| `$mapFrom` | **${mapFrom}** |\n| `$mapTo` | **${mapTo}** |\n\nDrag the time filter on the map: these follow ~300 ms after it comes to rest, and the URL gains `var-mapFrom` / `var-mapTo`.\n\n**The thing to watch is the histogram.** It must not rescale, and the handles must not jump — the data behind it is never re-queried, because the panel's own query still uses the dashboard time range. Narrow the window, then widen it again: everything is still there. In `bidirectional` mode that widening is impossible, which is the whole reason this mode exists.\n\nThe dashboard time picker must stay on 07:00–10:20 no matter what the slider does."
      },
      "title": "Published window",
      "type": "text"
    }
